  "tree_id": "f5cc822036c6da927926289847a8cb6d13aeb84e",
  "message": "P1b (2/3): rules, eval runner and lab sources (#5)\n\n* Add the rule-based diagnoser and the offline analysis\n\n- core/rules: the 29 rules of SPEC 10 in generic.py, python.py,\n  docker.py and terraform.py, and an engine that builds one match per\n  rule and ranks them by priority, confidence and earliest line. Rules\n  can look at the job conclusion, the end of the step, the step name,\n  or refine their category; unknown with confidence 0 when none fires.\n- core/analysis.py: excerpts (rule patterns flag error lines), rules,\n  the rules diagnosis and the signature for the failed jobs of a run.\n- One fixture file per rule with positive and negative sections; a test\n  fails when a rule lacks either.\n- pre-commit skips lab/, whose files fail lint on purpose.\n\n* Add the eval runner, the lab sources and the capture command\n\n- python -m evals run: loads evals/cases, runs the rules variant (all\n  runs what exists and lists the rest) and writes JSON and Markdown\n  reports with accuracy, per-category scores, the confusion matrix,\n  evidence, abstention, calibration, latency and cost.\n- lab/: 23 workflow_dispatch workflows that fail on purpose, two or\n  more per category, with a manifest of their expected diagnoses. It is\n  excluded from ruff and mypy.\n- python -m evals capture: through the user's gh login, turns failed\n  lab runs into redacted, labelled cases; --all skips runs already\n  captured.\n- Acceptance tests over the captured lab cases, skipped until there are\n  some.\n\n* Record D-60 and D-61 and align SPEC, README and CLAUDE.md with the rules and evals",
  "timestamp": "2026-11-14T00:51:51Z",
